# Template for local secrets: copy to .env and fill in (ADR 0018, 0044).
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored; values are provisioned by a human only (ADR 0046).
#
# NOTE: the ${...} references in .mcp.json are expanded from the environment that
# launches your MCP client (Claude Code), so load the file before starting it, e.g.:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a; claude
# or use direnv (`dotenv` line in .envrc).

# Supabase MCP server — least-privilege personal access token:
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# GitHub MCP server (.mcp.json `github`, official first-party endpoint). Expanded
# into the Authorization header at MCP-client launch, exactly like the tokens above
# (env-reference, never a literal — ADR 0044). INERT until provisioned: the server
# simply fails to connect without it, so it stays off like the Chromatic token.
# Use a FINE-GRAINED personal access token, least-privilege (ADR 0044/0046) — for
# reads of this repo's PRs/issues/Actions, Contents+Pull requests+Issues: read is
# enough; do not grant write scopes the agent doesn't need. Human-provisioned (ADR 0046).
# GITHUB_MCP_PAT=

# Set in bootstrap Phase 7, once the cloud Supabase project exists:
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=

# Set in bootstrap Phase 11, once the Chromatic project exists:
# CHROMATIC_APP_ID=
# CHROMATIC_PROJECT_TOKEN=

# Set in bootstrap Phase 12, to enable the advisory AI-process jobs (ADRs
# 0047-0057: AI code-review, CI-failure triage, changelog, security layer-2,
# Renovate triage). INERT until provisioned - the jobs stay off without it,
# exactly like the Chromatic token. In CI it is read as
# ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }} (env-reference, never a literal - ADR 0044);
# least-privilege, human-only (ADR 0046).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Model for the advisory AI jobs (scripts/ai/*). Defaults to claude-opus-4-8 when
# unset. Use claude-haiku-4-5 for the cheapest/fastest tier; claude-sonnet-4-6 for a
# middle option. The scripts only send adaptive-thinking + `effort` to models that
# support them (Opus 4.6-4.8 / Sonnet 4.6 / Fable 5), so Haiku/Sonnet-4.5 just work.
# In CI this is a GitHub Actions VARIABLE (not a secret): Settings → Secrets and
# variables → Actions → Variables → ANTHROPIC_MODEL. ANTHROPIC_EFFORT (low|medium|
# high|max, default high) is an optional companion, ignored on models without effort.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=

# ── Application env: .env.local (ADR 0018) ────────────────────────────────────
# App configuration is Zod-validated: public NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars in
# src/lib/env.ts, server-only secrets in src/lib/env.server.ts. Next.js reads
# overrides from .env.local (gitignored), with per-environment values living in
# Vercel.
#
# `npm run dev` (scripts/dev.mjs) resolves .env.local for you:
#   • LINKED to Vercel (`vercel login` + `vercel link`) → it runs
#     `vercel env pull` to sync the project's development environment.
#   • NOT linked → MANUAL FALLBACK: the app still runs on the local defaults
#     baked into src/lib/env.ts (local Supabase + http://localhost:3000). To
#     point at something else, hand-author .env.local using the keys below.
#
# This file (.env.example) is the template for both .env (host/MCP env, above)
# and any manual .env.local you create — copy the lines you need.

# Absolute origin the app is served from; defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# Production origin: https://claude-code-next-starter-two.vercel.app (set per environment
# in Vercel, not here):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Supabase (ADR 0012, 0018). The public vars default to the LOCAL stack in env.ts, so
# `npm run dev` / e2e work against `supabase start` with no setup. Override these
# only to point at a different instance; set real per-environment values in
# Vercel. Get the local values any time with `npx supabase status` (API_URL,
# PUBLISHABLE_KEY) — they are not pasted here so the secret scan stays clean.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
#
# Secret key — bypasses RLS; server-only (src/lib/env.server.ts), never public.
# Unset by default; needed only for admin operations. Local value from
# `supabase status` (SECRET_KEY); production value provisioned in Vercel:
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
